                <pb facs="0168" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg64"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Libertad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 8, 1890</date>.
                        (Received August 8.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Mizner informs Mr. Blaine that during a battle in the city of San Salvador
                    General Ezeta’s forces seized the United States consulate, hauled down the flag,
                    damaged some and destroyed other property. He reports that he has demanded
                    immediate reparation, and that a firmer manner is needed towards Guatemala and
                    Salvador and a stronger American naval force in Central American waters.</p>
            </div>
